---
# Mirrors the cpp-coding-standards skill's references/coding-style.md:
# Google C++ Style Guide baseline, with 4-space indentation, a 120-column
# limit, pointers/references bound to the type, one blank line between
# definitions, and one-line bodies only for functions defined in a class.
BasedOnStyle: Google
Standard: c++20

IndentWidth: 4
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
AccessModifierOffset: -4
ColumnLimit: 120

PointerAlignment: Left
ReferenceAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false

BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements

MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 1
SeparateDefinitionBlocks: Always
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
